  "pre_source_expected_claims": [
    "For every actual input-occurrence policy with strict sides at most floor(n/2), every valid-rank execution at fuel>=n has an actual positive Halves trace, including early equal termination and duplicates.",
    "Actual trace yields n<=W<=2*n, positive active count, and trace.length-1<=Nat.log 2 n<=Nat.clog 2 n. Singleton n1 has exactly one active invocation and zero edges.",
    "If actual measured pivot construction costs <=A*n+B at every nonempty state, the actual selector charge satisfies W<=T<=(A+4)*W+(B+5)*entries, and hence n<=T<=(2*(A+4)+2*(B+5))*n for halving policies. No assumed trace or free pivot search.",
    "Concrete median pivot first executes measured length for the lower-occurrence index then actual measured Selection.selectRun, charging its wrapper entry. Its value is ordered[(n-1)/2], whose duplicate-aware count bounds prove both strict sides halve.",
    "The actual concrete median callback has exact cost n+2+selectRun_cost at that index. A single linear constant exists before the payload type/list/rank/fuel; the source selector uniform bound discharges the callback contract.",
    "No changes to existing public one-based selector, optional values, prior proofs or tariffs. All new execution ranks are the existing zero-based book convention."
  ],
